From: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Date: Fri, 29 Nov 2024 17:11:33 +0800
Subject: crypto: sig - Set maskset to CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_MASK
Patch-mainline: v6.14-rc1
Git-commit: f04be1dddc70fcdd01497d66786e748106271eb6
References: jsc#PED-15972

As sig is now a standalone type, it no longer needs to have a wide
mask that includes akcipher.

Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Acked-by: Nicolai Stange <nstange@suse.de>
---
 crypto/sig.c |    4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/crypto/sig.c
+++ b/crypto/sig.c
@@ -17,8 +17,6 @@
 
 #include "internal.h"
 
-#define CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SIG_MASK	0x0000000e
-
 static const struct crypto_type crypto_sig_type;
 
 static void crypto_sig_exit_tfm(struct crypto_tfm *tfm)
@@ -80,7 +78,7 @@ static const struct crypto_type crypto_s
 	.report = crypto_sig_report,
 #endif
 	.maskclear = ~CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_MASK,
-	.maskset = CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SIG_MASK,
+	.maskset = CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_MASK,
 	.type = CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SIG,
 	.tfmsize = offsetof(struct crypto_sig, base),
 };
